    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d96-a2">

                <pb facs="0199" n="129" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg129"/>

                <head>Earl Russell to Mr.
                        Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Foreign Office,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-06-25"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >June</hi> 25, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your letter of the 23d instant, calling attention to a steam vessel which you
                    state is now fitting out at Liverpool with the intention of carrying on
                    hostilities against the government of the United States, and I have to acquaint
                    you that I have lost no time in referring the matter to the proper department of
                    her Majesty’s government.</p>
                <p>I have the honor to be, with the highest consideration, sir, your most obedient,
                    humble servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>RUSSELL.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
